  "title": "James M NDE 30595",
  "date": "June 20th, 1954",
  "content": "My fiancé was training as a nurse in Edmonton, Alberta when I was transferred to Winnipeg at the beginning of 1954. We were engaged to be married in September after her graduation in May. On June 5, 1954. I received news that my father had died of a heart attack. I immediately applied for and was granted ten days' vacation. I travelled by train to my parents' home. There, I took charge of the funeral arrangements, and moved my mother and her belongings to Edmonton. I settled the estate and returned to Winnipeg by train and resumed my duties.",
